            <ArticleTitle>Visceral surgery and pregnancy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e129-35</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jviscsurg.2010.07.005</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>With an incidence of 950,000 pregnancies per year in France, the likelihood of seeing one or more surgical abdominal diseases during pregnancy is high. The goal of this update was to describe the management of four different settings in the pregnant woman: colorectal cancer, laparoscopic surgery, gastrointestinal emergency surgery, and bariatric surgery.</AbstractText>
